{"c":[{"id":"66b7d7e70abf08e9","sum":"B21-22: planRequest window by {pid,number,title} or windowId; posted keys skip an inactive app's key equivalents; a consumer connection is a host session (evals call hostConnected); grant revoked on pause/stop; mutation runs: swift test --build-path /tmp.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2f09076641c97656","sum":"B21: planRequest names a window by {pid,number,title} or windowId, never both (unread = unseenWindow); rebuild caret-screen after mutated swift tests; posted keys skip an inactive app's key equivalents; Return in a frontmost one-line field presses the default button, unreported.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"09ccc8ad4b5ca18a","sum":"planRequest names its window by {pid, number, title} or windowId, never both; unread = unseenWindow, neither = ScreenModel.userWindow (v2/host planError needs an unseenWindow sentence). swift test on mutated source rebuilds .build/debug/caret-screen: rebuild before GUI evals.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T015937Z-41933c0bb214864e","text":"planRequest names its window as window {pid, number, title} or windowId, never both; an unread one is unseenWindow; neither means the frontmost app's last focused window (ScreenModel.userWindow). v2/host's planError switch needs an unseenWindow sentence (B21).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T015937Z-53ebaedecebf757b","text":"swift test on a mutated source rebuilds .build/debug/caret-screen; rebuild from the restored source before any GUI eval runs those binaries (B21 caught it by timestamp).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f69cdfcee30c7eb9","sum":"B21: keys posted to an inactive app's pid skip AppKit key equivalents (posted Return never ran the default button, Space pressed a focused one); frontmost, Return in a single-line field presses the default button, which the reader does not report.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T015937Z-ebf44f31f7890c91","text":"A key posted to a pid whose app is not active skips AppKit key equivalents: the fixture's default button never ran on posted Return or Enter (0 of 10), Space pressed a focused button 5 of 5. The reader places key presses from cached focus and default button (B21).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T031707Z-b7d2054c5f965771","text":"AppKit presses a window's default button on Return typed into a single-line text field: frontmost fixture, Note focused, Send ran 5 of 5. B21's reader counts no Return while a text field has focus (brief), so that submit goes unreported (gui/keys-front).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9b3d66084a009c9f","sum":"B22: a consumer connection is a host session (tasks revoked on close; evals call helper.hostConnected); pause/stop/settings/disconnect revoke the act grant at once, Helper.authorize before each act; mutation runs use swift test --build-path /tmp, grep 'recorded an issue'.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"dc5a5754f076b1b1","sum":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; tasks bind to it and are revoked when it closes; in-process evals must call helper.hostConnected(id). Pause, stop, settings and disconnect revoke the act grant at once; Helper.authorize is asked before each act.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150809Z-35454632bb9daf62","text":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; accepted tasks bind to the one that started them and are revoked when it closes; runs with no Tab need a connected host. In-process tests and evals that play the host must call helper.hostConnected(id) or no skill runs on its own.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150824Z-0b7169f06df102c4","text":"B22: every pause, take over, stop, Caret pause, settings/permission/skill/memory change and host disconnect revokes the act grant at once (Executor.revoke/recheck); the executor also asks Helper.authorize right before each write, press, raise and calendar add.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ccdfe7e5f11e70bf","sum":"B22: a consumer connection is a host session (tasks revoked when it closes; evals call helper.hostConnected). Mutation runs: swift test --build-path /tmp/... keeps .build/debug clean; Swift Testing prints 'recorded an issue' for a failure, grep that.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150829Z-581618fb20568b53","text":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; accepted tasks bind to the session that started them and are revoked when it closes; runs with no Tab need a connected host. In-process tests and evals that play the host must call helper.hostConnected(id).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150830Z-a3b40432646c1572","text":"B22: swift test --build-path /tmp/... keeps mutation runs out of .build/debug; Swift Testing marks failures 'recorded an issue', not ✘, so grep that when checking a mutation was caught.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b90f59e8e9d017fa","sum":"B22-B23: --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS; presses only SAFE_PRESSES; only a hello with host: true is the host; undo marks give notSameElement; reader needs a 0700 socket dir and helperAuth first (launch.ts, --auth-fd); crash eval SIGKILLs a helper mid run.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e0ee3433a46919d2","sum":"B22-D2-03: --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only; presses only whole SAFE_PRESSES labels (risk.ts, RiskTable, press-risk.json together). Open-time event card is needsYou; only a hello with host: true is the host (evals: hostConnected).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8d97b0b1c518449c","sum":"B22: --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only; window ids are opaque to the helper. Presses only whole SAFE_PRESSES labels, never in a system prompt; change risk.ts, RiskTable.safePresses and press-risk.json together.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150830Z-cd56cc67608f9643","text":"B22: --act-pids now needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only and caret-fixture pids; window ids are <pid>-<start µs>-<generation>-<n>, opaque to the helper.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150843Z-b8f6b3671dd764ee","text":"B22: presses only whole labels in risk.ts SAFE_PRESSES / RiskTable.safePresses, never in a system prompt (subrole AXSystemDialog or AXSystemFloatingWindow, or a TCC/SecurityAgent process); change both lists and press-risk.json together.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e926b62b147229c0","sum":"D2-03: an open-time event card is needsYou with choices; a closed-line Tab re-offers it under a new key. B23: only a consumer hello with host: true is the host (v2/host must send it or no skill runs alone); in-process evals call helper.hostConnected(id).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T153943Z-e96b8d822d84ddbb","text":"D2-03: an event card whose time is open (no AM/PM, no end) is figure needsYou with a choices block; the host's closed-line Tab sends no variants row, so the helper adds nothing and re-offers the card under a new key (offerWithdrawn reoffered).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171742Z-0e49751b5685c975","text":"B23: only a consumer hello with host: true counts as the host; other consumers bind their own work but keep no run with no Tab alive. v2/host must send host: true, or no skill runs on its own. In-process evals still call helper.hostConnected(id).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c7edb83e11969db2","sum":"B23: undo sends sameAs with a mark (reader: notSameElement otherwise; fakes test/fake-marks.ts); crash-recovery-eval SIGKILLs a helper mid run. Reader needs a 0700 socket dir; caret-screen needs --auth-fd and helperAuth first (launch.ts; evals --auth-fd 0).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"200602a89c015e6e","sum":"B23: undo sends sameAs with a mark; the reader answers notSameElement unless the element is the one it wrote (fakes: test/fake-marks.ts). crash-recovery-eval.ts SIGKILLs a real helper mid skill run; its 'helper still running' check catches crashes after the last publish.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171742Z-101e1e3d273eec2a","text":"B23: forward value writes carry a mark and undo sends sameAs; the reader answers notSameElement unless the element at the key is the one it wrote (per app worker, gone on reader restart). Test fakes use test/fake-marks.ts; marks.replace(windowId, key) plays a replaced field.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171742Z-362dd90f069eee83","text":"B23: scripts/crash-recovery-eval.ts SIGKILLs a real helper child mid skill run while the script plays reader and host; its 'restarted helper is still running' check is what catches a crash after the last publish (an id collision did exactly that).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cf937cd80d01ef87","sum":"B23: the reader connects only to a 0700 socket dir of the user's own (tests: mkdtemp). caret-screen needs --auth-fd (32-byte secret) and trusts a helper whose first line is helperAuth (HMAC challenge+pid); use launch.ts; evals pass --auth-fd 0 and sendSecret.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171742Z-7971f1eeb5bd9db9","text":"B23: the reader connects only to a socket whose directory is 0700 and the user's own (never /tmp itself; HelperServer chmods its dir). Tests and evals put sockets in mkdtemp directories.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171817Z-c0fbce2e0a5b8f78","text":"B23: caret-screen needs --auth-fd (32-byte secret) and trusts only a helper whose first line is helperAuth (HMAC of challenge+pid, pid = LOCAL_PEERPID). Use helper/src/launch.ts; evals pass --auth-fd 0, sendSecret(reader, s), new HelperServer(..., s).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
